module gunbc.observation_emit_census

import std.types { String, NonEmptyStr, Bool, List }
import std.dissolution { DissolutionCondition, unbound_dissolution, dissolution_description }
import std.nat { Nat }
import std.disposition { Disposition, Terminal, Scaffold, SingleAuthority }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

// P3 of the progress-and-observation lane: the census wall. Every place the floor emits a progress
// line today is either a PROJECTION of the observation event stream (migrated, P1/P2) or a COUNTED
// FRONTIER ROW carrying a reason and a dissolve-on — the same discipline the site subsumption lane
// uses for unthemed colours. This module is the census authority: the classification is a closed
// sum, so a site cannot be half-classified, and the roster below names the structured-tag emit
// families that exist in the seed today. The executable hygiene witness is bidirectional: it reds
// when a rostered marker vanishes AND when a known live tag family is missing from the roster, so
// growth after the snapshot cannot silently understate.

// Sequencing, per the operator ruling and live-log review (run 30142403230): tagged migrations
// landed (gantt, governor, typecheck-attribution, measurement, shell with named-intent subjects;
// Ambient ShellTrace Suppressed at Normal). Post-census growth tags ([floor-drain], [receipt],
// [file], and #7205's [resolve-split]/[assembly-split]) are CountedFrontierSite rows so the roster
// cannot silently understate. [gate-warm-cost] and [witness-row-cost-drift] were rows here until
// 2026-08-11, and #7284's [witness-row-cost-migration-disclosure] until 2026-08-22, each leaving
// when its raw emit was deleted outright rather than migrated. [floor-memory] LEFT THE ROSTER ON
// 2026-08-26 AND IT IS NOT ONE OF THESE DEPARTURES, WHICH IS THE FINDING. The marker and its
// render_heartbeat_line_mirror are gone from the seed (measured: no occurrence of either anywhere
// under src/, only one doc comment naming the mirror), and read no further that looks exactly like
// the three retirements above -- an emit deleted at the root, a row simply absent. It is the
// opposite. The floor still emits a periodic progress line and a per-claim RSS growth line; they
// are now [floor-heartbeat] and [floor-claim-memory], raw formatted eprintlns in cli_run.rs with no
// projection behind them. So a MIGRATED row's projection was DELETED and raw emits took over its
// job under new names -- a reversal, not a retirement. Both successors are on the roster above as
// CountedFrontierSite, which moves the frontier count UP by two. THE NEAR-MISS IS WHY THIS IS
// WRITTEN AT LENGTH: the row was first deleted as a completed retirement on the evidence that its
// marker was gone, and marker-absence is exactly as consistent with a reversal as with a
// retirement. The census cannot tell them apart by looking at the row that vanished; only by asking
// what now does the job. That question is not asked by any check here, and it is a second face of
// the same missing discovery the completeness note names -- an unrostered successor is invisible
// for precisely the reason an unrostered new family is. THIS NOTE PREVIOUSLY GROUNDED
// [witness-row-cost] ON `claim_executor discovery_claim_result`, AND THAT FUNCTION DOES NOT EXIST
// -- not renamed, not moved: no declaration by that name is anywhere in the seed, and the surviving
// [witness-row-cost] refusals are the witness_cost_* helpers in cli_run.rs. The citation was
// fabricated at the moment it was written, in the same 2026-08-22 change that restored the row on a
// correct premise, and it was copied from here into
// test.claim.observation_raw_print_retirement_acceptance_test, so one invented symbol became two
// files' evidence. The family is still live and still on the roster; only the symbol naming its
// occurrence was false.

type EmitSiteDisposition
  = MigratedToObservation { via: NonEmptyStr }
  | CountedFrontierSite { reason: NonEmptyStr, dissolution: DissolutionCondition }

// A closed sum, so a site is exactly one of two things and never silently neither.
// MigratedToObservation names the projection that replaced the raw emit — the evidence the site now
// speaks the event vocabulary. CountedFrontierSite carries a reason it has not migrated yet and the
// trigger that will dissolve it, so the debt is countable and prioritizable rather than an
// open-ended intention. There is no third arm, which is the point: an emit site the census has not
// looked at cannot be represented here, so the roster's completeness is what the witness checks
// against the seed.

// WHO PRODUCES A FAMILY AND WHO CONSUMES IT ARE CENSUS FACTS, NOT PROSE (2026-09-11, the
// observability lane's census extension). A row that says only "migrated" or "frontier" cannot
// answer the two questions the brief of that lane put first: which declaration emits the line, and
// whether anything downstream PARSES it -- because a family whose reader is a machine has a wire
// contract, and cutting its producer over to the observation vocabulary without cutting the reader
// silently breaks the reader while the census books progress. The producer is a DeclarationRef
// into the hand-Rust namespace (v1_compiler.cli_run and siblings), which the ingestion citation
// wall counts as outside-index rather than refusing (gunbc.declaration_index_seed_growth), so a
// deleted producer is at least a countable outside-index row rather than a silent lie, and a
// witness below holds each named producer's SYMBOL present in the seed sources. Consumption has
// exactly three honest answers. MachineConsumed names the reader declaration and the fields whose
// values change its behaviour, so a producer cut knows what it must preserve. HumanPresentationOnly
// carries the EVIDENCE for the claim, which must be more than "a grep for the prefix found no
// parser" -- that search proves absence only over the population it searched, and the brief
// forbids booking human-only on it. ConsumerUnresolved records what WAS searched and is the
// default for every row until a real reader survey lands; it is not a defect state, it is the
// honest one, and observation_emit_unresolved_consumer_count folds it so it can rank. THE PRODUCER
// IS ONE DECLARATION PER FAMILY, AT FUNCTION GRAIN: a family with several emitting sites ([floor-drain]
// has seven across five functions and two files) names one of them, and the enumeration of the rest
// is the same occurrence-grain discovery the completeness note below records as unbuilt. A row
// names a producer that exists today; it does not claim to name every site.
type EmitProducer
  = ProducerDeclared { declaration: DeclarationRef }
  | ProducerUnlocated { reason: NonEmptyStr }

type EmitConsumption
  = MachineConsumed { reader: DeclarationRef, fields_read: List<NonEmptyStr> }
  | HumanPresentationOnly { evidence: NonEmptyStr }
  | ConsumerUnresolved { searched: NonEmptyStr }

type CensusedEmitSite {
  marker: NonEmptyStr
  producer: EmitProducer
  consumption: EmitConsumption
  disposition: EmitSiteDisposition
}

fn seed_producer(decl_name: String) -> EmitProducer {
  ProducerDeclared { declaration: DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: decl_name, field: WholeDeclaration } }
}

fn seed_producer_in(module_path: String, decl_name: String) -> EmitProducer {
  ProducerDeclared { declaration: DeclarationRef { module_path: module_path, decl_name: decl_name, field: WholeDeclaration } }
}

// The in-repo reader search every row below was subjected to on 2026-09-11: every file under the
// repository outside the producer's own file, for the family's tag spelling, excluding target/ and
// .git/. It found no parser for any family. That is evidence about THIS REPOSITORY'S sources and
// nothing else -- operator scripts, dashboards and log post-processors outside the tree are
// unsurveyed -- so every row stays ConsumerUnresolved rather than human-only, per the brief.
data in_repo_reader_search: NonEmptyStr = "in-repo source search 2026-09-11 for the tag spelling outside the producer file: no parser found; readers outside this repository (operator scripts, dashboards, log post-processors) unsurveyed" as NonEmptyStr

fn unresolved_after_in_repo_search() -> EmitConsumption {
  ConsumerUnresolved { searched: in_repo_reader_search }
}

// A ROW NAMES A TAG FAMILY, NOT A FILE, AND THE FIELD THAT NAMED A FILE IS DELETED (2026-08-26).
// CensusedEmitSite carried source_file: NonEmptyStr, whose sole consumer anywhere in the corpus was
// the witness's census_marker_present, which read that one file and grepped it. That is a
// positional citation in the sense §3 rules against -- a second naming scheme for something the
// seed already contains -- and it rots in the one way this census cannot tolerate: it goes false
// when the emit MOVES, which is not a census fact at all. It did. #9228 deleted claim_executor's
// unreachable plan/walk surface (21,366 -> 11,508 lines) and the file-pinned rows went red five at
// once -- floor-memory, receipt, resolve-split, assembly-split, witness-row-cost -- of which
// exactly ONE was a real census event (floor-memory's emit left the seed, and its row is deleted
// accordingly) and four were the pin rotting while the tag family sat untouched in a sibling seed
// file. A check whose red says `the code moved` where the census asks `does this still emit` is
// measuring the wrong quantity, and four false reds beside one true one is worse than no check,
// because the true one is indistinguishable in the noise. What replaces it is seed_emit_sources
// below: presence is searched across the SEED, so a marker that moves between seed files stays
// green and a marker that leaves the seed reds. The denominator became the thing the census is
// actually about.

data seed_emit_sources: List<String> = [
  "src/v1/stage0/src/bin/claim_executor.rs",
  "src/v1/stage0/src/bin/claim_batch.rs",
  "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs",
  "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/required_floor_runner.rs",
  "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/entry_resolve.rs",
  "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/declared_refs.rs",
  "src/v1/stage0/src/pre_push.rs",
  "src/v1/stage0/src/v1_interpreter.rs",
  "src/v1/stage0/src/v1_rt.rs",
  "src/v1/stage0/src/memory_governor.rs"
]

// THE DENOMINATOR FELL BEHIND THE SEED AND THE PREDICTED NARROW HAPPENED (2026-09-11). cli_run.rs
// was split into cli_run/*.rs submodules after this list was written, and the emits moved with the
// code: [floor-claim-memory] lives only in cli_run/required_floor_runner.rs and one [floor-drain]
// arm in cli_run/entry_resolve.rs. Neither file was listed, so census_marker_present answered
// FALSE for floor_claim_memory_site -- a rostered row whose marker the census could not find --
// and nothing reported it, because the witness that asks is declined by the floor
// (test.claim.observation_emit_census_witness_test declares ReadsLiveTree). Measured by listing
// every seed file containing a bracket-tagged eprintln; the four files added above are the
// difference. This is the second time a declined witness held a false heartbeat-family row
// (test.claim.observation_lockstep_witness_test records the first), and the fix is the same each
// time: the denominator is re-derived by hand until the source-derived discovery this note names
// lands.

// THE CENSUS'S DENOMINATOR: the seed files a tagged progress emit can live in. Presence of a
// rostered marker is asked of this SET, never of one named file, which is what makes a row survive
// #9228-shaped code movement and red only when the tag family actually leaves the seed. THIS LIST
// IS ITSELF HAND-MAINTAINED AND THAT IS THE RESIDUE, stated rather than hidden: a seed file dropped
// from it narrows the search silently, which is the empty-observation narrow this repository names
// as strictly worse than a widen. It is mitigated, not closed -- the witness asserts every listed
// source reads non-empty, so a path that stops existing reds instead of quietly contributing
// nothing, and the list is one authority for the whole census rather than a pin per row, so it
// cannot rot thirteen different ways. What would close it is the source-derived denominator both
// this module's witness and the retirement acceptance already name as their residue: the seed's
// tagged emits DISCOVERED at occurrence grain from syntax, joined against this roster, reporting
// live-but-unrostered and rostered-but-absent simultaneously. That discovery is unbuilt, and until
// it lands this list is the honest approximation of it.

data floor_heartbeat_site: CensusedEmitSite = CensusedEmitSite {
  marker: "[floor-heartbeat]" as NonEmptyStr,
  producer: seed_producer(decl_name: "spawn_floor_heartbeat"),
  consumption: unresolved_after_in_repo_search(),
  disposition: MigratedToObservation {
    via: "gunbc.observation_ci_render.ci_heartbeat_line (seed seed_heartbeat_line; mirror render_heartbeat_line_mirror; RunSegment+PhaseSegment subject from the floor seam; every /proc and cgroup reading a Measured arm; stall clause by gunbc.memory_stall_refusal's own rate and share). RESTORED 2026-09-11: this row was a CountedFrontierSite from 2026-08-26, when #9228 deleted the [floor-memory] projection and a raw key=value eprintln took its job under this tag -- a migrated row that had silently reverted. The restoration replaced HeartbeatSample with the one-attempt floor's real sample rather than reviving the batch/entry shape, because the fields the raw line had grown (cpu delta, major faults, cgroup charge and throttle events, host vmstat, the stall window) each carried a measured justification the old record could not hold. The raw key=value shape is gone from the seed; the marker survives as the FLOOR_HEARTBEAT_CENSUS_MARKER const so this row cannot go stale. The reader question is what the consumption field carries: the old line had no in-repo parser, and this cut did not survey readers outside the tree, so if one existed it now reads prose" as NonEmptyStr
  }
}

data floor_claim_memory_site: CensusedEmitSite = CensusedEmitSite {
  marker: "[floor-claim-memory]" as NonEmptyStr,
  producer: seed_producer(decl_name: "run_required_floor"),
  consumption: unresolved_after_in_repo_search(),
  disposition: CountedFrontierSite {
    reason: "the per-claim and worst-claim RSS growth lines emitted beside the heartbeat, raw and formatted in cli_run/required_floor_runner.rs with no observation projection behind them. Same family as [floor-heartbeat] and the same 2026-08-26 regression; the heartbeat half was restored on 2026-09-11 and this half was deliberately left for a separate cut, because a growth line is a DELTA between two RSS readings on a named claim and the renderer has no measurement-delta projection yet -- ci_measurement_rss_line carries one level, not a change. The 2026-08-26 note that this row's marker was present in the seed was FALSE from the cli_run split until 2026-09-11: the emit lives in a file the census denominator did not list (see the note on seed_emit_sources)" as NonEmptyStr,
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(description: "a measurement-delta projection in gunbc.observation_ci_render (a MeasurementSegment carrying the RSS before, after and the claim identity) rendered by a seed mirror on the same oracle pattern as the heartbeat, at which point this row becomes MigratedToObservation")
  }
}

